# Keep the build context small. Both images take the root of the workspace as
# their context — .devcontainer/Dockerfile.ros2 for vcpkg.json, docker/Dockerfile
# for vcpkg.json and src/ — so anything listed here is excluded from both.
#
# Nothing that either Dockerfile copies may appear below: vcpkg.json, src/ and
# docker/entrypoint.sh all have to stay.

# Build products of a host build. Copying them in would shadow the ones the
# image builds for its own architecture.
build/
install/
log/

# History, editor and tooling state: never read during a build.
.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# Documentation: not read by either build.
doc/
*.md

# Reference photographs of the assembled robot. They sit under src/, so
# docker/Dockerfile copies them into its builder stage, but they are not a ROS
# package and never reach the runtime image.
src/reference_img/

# Deliberately NOT excluded: src/hexapod_description/meshes/*.blend. It is large
# and nothing reads it at runtime, but install(DIRECTORY meshes) puts it in the
# package share directory, so dropping it here would quietly change what the
# image built by docker/Dockerfile ships.
